[statement]
A setgid directory shared through a named group, carrying an access and a
default control list, as GNU tar writes one. On extraction GNU tar keeps
setgid and bsdtar drops it (measured by extraction). Strict refuses it;
Compatible reads the header's mode, as GNU tar extracts it.

[archive]
pax SCHILY.acl.access=user::rwx,group::r-x,group:1000:rwx,mask::rwx,other::r-x SCHILY.acl.default=user::rwx,group::r-x,group:1000:rwx,mask::rwx,other::r-x
header name=d/ typeflag=5 mode=0o2775
header name=after
data "y"
end

